# Local Coding Preferences — Flint

This file is for my personal preferences and local Claude environment only.

## Responsibility Boundary

- Local files define personal coding taste, local tooling, and machine-specific commands.
- Project-specific behavior belongs in the project's own instructions.
- Keep this file generic enough to apply across repositories.

## Coding Taste

- Keep code simple, direct, and consistent with the surrounding project.
- Do not add fallback logic or defensive code unless explicitly asked or validating a real boundary: user input, external APIs, network edges, filesystem, or process boundaries.
- Fail fast. Do not swallow, downgrade, or silently ignore errors.
- Prefer clear names over comments. Comments should explain why, not what.
- Keep responsibilities narrow. Split functions or files when responsibility becomes unclear, not to satisfy a line count.
- Prefer immutability by default. Contain mutation when it is genuinely required.
- Prefer fewer dependencies. Add dependencies only when they clearly reduce real complexity.
- Delete dead code instead of polishing it.

## Verification

Choose the smallest meaningful check that proves the change.

